<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The accessibility service performs the system actions (lock, screenshot, Back, Home, Recents,
  notifications, quick settings, power menu), it can take the two volume keys, and it can see which
  app is in front. It draws only when the user asks: the bar everywhere, when they choose it to draw
  the bar (Visibility › Draw the bar with); the bar on the lock screen, when they turn on Show on the
  lock screen; and the button animation beside the volume buttons, when that is on. Drawing needs
  no event or flag here: its windows are TYPE_ACCESSIBILITY_OVERLAY. The live event subscription is
  set at runtime and is empty unless the user has picked apps to hide the bar in, given apps
  gestures of their own, or asked the button animation to answer the power menu; the types below
  are the most it will ever ask for.

  canRequestFilterKeyEvents is for the Quick panel's Instant volume keys and the button animation.
  The filter itself is requested at runtime and only while one of them is on; even then the service
  takes the two volume keys and hands every other key straight back.

  typeWindowStateChanged is for hiding the bar in apps the user picks and for gestures the user has
  changed for particular apps, and is subscribed only while there are any; and, with Instant volume
  keys, for the moment a Volume down press is undecided, when
  only the event's package is checked, to tell a Volume down + Power screenshot from a press; and,
  while the button animation answers the power button, to see the power menu come up, known by its
  window's package and class. The service reads which app's window came to the front, its package
  and class, and nothing inside it.

  canRetrieveWindowContent is false: the service never reads what is inside a window, this app's
  or any other's.

  isAccessibilityTool is false on purpose: this is a convenience feature for everyone, not an
  assistive tool, and the Play listing carries the matching disclosure.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/accessibility_service_description"
    android:summary="@string/accessibility_service_summary"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:notificationTimeout="100"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="false"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault"
    android:canPerformGestures="false"
    android:canRequestFilterKeyEvents="true"
    android:isAccessibilityTool="false" />
